1
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:53,500
Death has never been closer.

2
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Final Destination 5 is a horror, mystery film directed by Steven Quale.

3
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:28,500
Death is just as omnipresent as ever, and is unleashed after one man’s premonition
saves a group of coworkers from a terrifying suspension bridge collapse.

4
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:16,000
But this group of unsuspecting souls was never supposed to survive, and, in a terrifying race against time,
the ill-fated group frantically tries to discover a way to escape Death’s sinister agenda.

5
00:18:57,500 --> 00:19:03,500
Sam, played by Nicholas D'Agosto.

6
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:51,000
Molly, played by Emma Bell.

7
00:26:32,500 --> 00:26:38,500
Peter Friedkin, played by Miles Fisher.

8
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Candice Hooper, played by Ellen Wroe.

9
00:34:07,500 --> 00:34:13,500
Olivia Castle, played by Jacqueline MacInnes Wood.

10
00:37:55,000 --> 00:38:01,000
Isaac, played by P.J. Byrne.

11
00:41:42,500 --> 00:41:48,500
Final Destination 5 is a 2011 American 3D supernatural horror film
directed by Steven Quale and written by Eric Heisserer.

12
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
It is the fifth installment in the Final Destination film
series and a prequel to Final Destination (2000).

13
00:49:17,500 --> 00:49:23,500
Nicholas D'Agosto stars as a young man who has a premonition about a suspension bridge collapsing, and
saves a group of people from Death, only to learn that they cannot escape its plan.

14
00:53:05,000 --> 00:53:11,000
Emma Bell, Miles Fisher, Arlen Escarpeta, David Koechner,
and Tony Todd star in supporting roles.

15
00:56:52,500 --> 00:56:58,500
Despite The Final Destination (2009) being announced as the final film in the franchise, that film's
financial success led to the development of a fifth installment, which began in 2010.

16
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
Filming took place in Vancouver, as with the first three installments.

17
01:04:27,500 --> 01:04:33,500
It is the second film in the franchise to be shot in 3D.

18
01:08:15,000 --> 01:08:21,000
Final Destination 5 was theatrically released on August 12, 2011,
and on DVD on December 27, 2011, by Warner Bros.

19
01:12:02,500 --> 01:12:08,500
Pictures and New Line Cinema.

20
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:56,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $157 million worldwide,
becoming – as of May 2025 – the third highest-grossing film in the franchise.

21
01:19:37,500 --> 01:19:43,500
A sixth film, Final Destination Bloodlines, was released in May 2025.

22
01:23:25,000 --> 01:23:31,000
The film explores themes of premonition, accidental
death, crash, end is here, death.

23
01:27:12,500 --> 01:27:18,500
The tone is dark and mind_bending.
